  "semantics": [
    "Only exact AIR version 1 plus asyncTasks in both real initialize metadata grants controls; no Agent-name or binary-version branch.",
    "Task ID comes only from validated current connection/native session announcements. Raw protocol envelopes remain visible; raw replay and arbitrary history IDs grant no task action.",
    "Stop uses exact original asyncTaskId/sessionId on the existing connection. accepted/rejected/unknown are request observations; only official completed/failed/stopped state updates end task activity.",
    "Task stop does not cancel the reply, rewrite original tool or turn results, pause/consume waiting messages, or alter their existing send policy.",
    "Task activity retains the existing lifecycle work lease and participates in configuration/archive/delete/close guards. Cold automatic configuration restore now uses the same task busy state; confirmed terminal tasks retain ordinary restore behavior.",
    "Late and wrong-owner replies do not transfer ownership. Unknown state can accept its first same-owner terminal, including before spawn; conflicting tool ownership remains uncertain and blocks idle.",
    "512 total live task/early-state records bound memory. Overflow or conflicting ownership remains uncertain; no new persistent event/task ledger is introduced."
  ],
